  "usage_note": "The adverb is **properly**: *Do it properly*. *Do it proper* is heard only in very informal British speech. After **be**, **proper** usually means *polite* (sense 3): *It isn't proper*. Before a noun it usually means *right* or *real* (senses 1 and 2).",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "Please do your homework proper.",
      "correct": "Please do your homework properly.",
      "note": "After a verb, use the adverb **properly**."
    }
